        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>How much does a virtual assistant cost per month? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">A full-time dedicated virtual assistant typically costs $1,200 to $2,500 a month all in, depending on role and experience. Part-time freelance support runs $400 to $1,200 a month for 10 to 20 hours a week, and US agency hours at $35 to $60 an hour can exceed $3,000 a month at the same volume.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Why is there such a wide price range? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">Because the models bundle different things. A $10 hourly freelancer gives you raw hours and all the hiring risk. A dedicated professional through a partner includes recruiting, vetting, employment, payroll, compliance, and a replacement guarantee inside one monthly rate.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Is a cheaper virtual assistant ever the better deal? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">For small, clearly defined tasks with low cost of failure, yes. For roles that touch customers, finances, or your calendar, the cheapest rate usually becomes the most expensive option after the first failed hire or missed week.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Do I pay recruitment or placement fees on top? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">With Remote Team Partners, no. Recruitment is included in the monthly rate, with no separate placement fees. Some agencies charge one to two months of salary as a placement fee, so always ask before signing.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>What does a dedicated professional cost at Remote Team Partners? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">One monthly rate per professional, scoped to the role and seniority you need and quoted exactly on a discovery call. One invoice per professional covers salary, employment, payroll, and compliance.</div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
